   "stem_html": "<figure id=\"fig7_55\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2631e90c078aeb86.png\" alt=\"Map of the United States showing the electoral vote outcomes in 1860. Lincoln won California (4), Oregon (3), Minnesota (4), Iowa (4), Wisconsin (5), Illinois (11), Michigan (6), Indiana (13), Ohio (23), Pennsylvania (27), New York (35), New Jersey (4), and all of New England, including Vermont (5), New Hampshire (5), Maine (8), Massachusetts (13), Rhode Island (4), and Connecticut (6). Douglas won Missouri (9). Breckinridge won Texas (4), Louisiana (6), Arkansas (4), Mississippi (7), Alabama (9), Georgia (10), Florida (3), Maryland (8), Delaware (3), North Carolina (10), and South Carolina (8). Bell won Virginia (12), Kentucky (12), and Tennessee (12).\">\n<figcaption>Electoral map from the 1860 presidential election.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the map provided.</i></p>\n<p>The electoral results shown in the map best demonstrate the influence of</p>",
